('<div class="kicker reveal">Sotto il cofano</div>','<div class="kicker reveal">Under the hood</div>'),
('Tutto è un file.<br><span class="grad-text">Tutto si estende.</span>','Everything is a file.<br><span class="grad-text">Everything extends.</span>'),
('<span class="d">13 ruoli senior (prompt, modello, tool)</span>','<span class="d">13 senior roles (prompt, model, tools)</span>'),
('<span class="d">comandi: feature, review, debug,</span>','<span class="d">commands: feature, review, debug,</span>'),
('<span class="d">+ conoscenza: definition-of-done,</span>','<span class="d">+ knowledge: definition-of-done,</span>'),
('<span class="d">test degli hook</span>','<span class="d">hook tests</span>'),
('<h4>➕ Nuovo ruolo</h4><p>Aggiungi <span class="inline-code">agents/&lt;ruolo&gt;.md</span> copiando la sezione "Team protocol", poi aggiungilo alla tabella nella skill <span class="inline-code">feature</span>.</p>','<h4>➕ New role</h4><p>Add <span class="inline-code">agents/&lt;role&gt;.md</span> copying the "Team protocol" section, then add it to the table in the <span class="inline-code">feature</span> skill.</p>'),
('<h4>📚 Nuove convenzioni di stack</h4><p>Una skill <span class="inline-code">skills/stack-&lt;nome&gt;/SKILL.md</span> con una <span class="inline-code">description</span> precisa su quando usarla: gli agenti la caricano da soli quando serve.</p>','<h4>📚 New stack conventions</h4><p>A <span class="inline-code">skills/stack-&lt;name&gt;/SKILL.md</span> skill with a precise <span class="inline-code">description</span> of when to use it: agents load it on their own when needed.</p>'),
('<h4>🔁 Dopo ogni modifica</h4>','<h4>🔁 After every change</h4>'),
('<span class="d"># alza "version" in plugin.json, poi</span>','<span class="d"># bump "version" in plugin.json, then</span>'),
# ---- faq
('<h2 class="reveal d1">Domande frequenti</h2>','<h2 class="reveal d1">Frequently asked questions</h2>'),
('<summary>Devo usare tutti e 13 gli agenti ogni volta?</summary><p>No, ed è voluto. Il lead attiva solo i ruoli che hanno un task — di solito 3–5. Per un lavoro piccolo te lo dice e lo fa da solo, perché un team costa più token di una sessione singola.</p>',
 '<summary>Do I have to use all 13 agents every time?</summary><p>No, by design. The lead only activates the roles that have a task — usually 3–5. For a small job it tells you and does it alone, because a team costs more tokens than a single session.</p>'),
('<summary>Come cambio il modello di un ruolo?</summary><p>Modifica <span class="inline-code">model:</span> nel frontmatter del file in <span class="inline-code">plugins/devteam/agents/</span>, oppure chiedi al lead un modello specifico quando lancia il team ("usa Opus anche per backend").</p>',
 '<summary>How do I change a role\'s model?</summary><p>Edit <span class="inline-code">model:</span> in the frontmatter of the file in <span class="inline-code">plugins/devteam/agents/</span>, or ask the lead for a specific model when it launches the team ("use Opus for backend too").</p>'),
('<summary>Il gate blocca ogni task, cosa succede?</summary><p>Probabilmente il progetto è "rosso" in partenza: typecheck, lint o test falliscono già prima che il team tocchi qualcosa. Sistemalo prima, oppure metti temporaneamente <span class="inline-code">"gateTasks": false</span> in <span class="inline-code">.claude/devteam.json</span>. Nel gate metti solo controlli veloci e affidabili: gli e2e li lancia <b>qa</b>.</p>',
 '<summary>The gate blocks every task, what\'s going on?</summary><p>The project is probably "red" to begin with: typecheck, lint or tests already fail before the team touches anything. Fix it first, or temporarily set <span class="inline-code">"gateTasks": false</span> in <span class="inline-code">.claude/devteam.json</span>. Only put fast, reliable checks in the gate: <b>qa</b> runs the e2e tests.</p>'),
('<summary>Posso parlare direttamente con un teammate?</summary><p>Sì. In modalità in-process: <span class="inline-code">↑/↓</span> per selezionarlo nel pannello agenti, <span class="inline-code">Invio</span> per aprirlo, <span class="inline-code">Ctrl+T</span> per la task list. In modalità auto dentro tmux o iTerm2 ogni teammate ha il suo pannello.</p>',
 '<summary>Can I talk to a teammate directly?</summary><p>Yes. In in-process mode: <span class="inline-code">↑/↓</span> to select it in the agents panel, <span class="inline-code">Enter</span> to open it, <span class="inline-code">Ctrl+T</span> for the task list. In auto mode inside tmux or iTerm2 every teammate gets its own pane.</p>'),
('<summary>Il team può fare push o deploy da solo?</summary><p>No. Il guardrail blocca force push, reset distruttivi,','<summary>Can the team push or deploy by itself?</summary><p>No. The guardrail blocks force pushes, destructive resets,'),
(', fastlane e simili. Il team prepara tutto — commit proposto, checklist di invio — e tu esegui.</p>',', fastlane and the like. The team prepares everything — proposed commit, submission checklist — and you execute.</p>'),
('<summary>Funziona con il mio stack?</summary><p>Il team è generico: legge il tuo <span class="inline-code">CLAUDE.md</span> e segue le convenzioni che trova. In più ha skill di conoscenza pronte per TypeScript, .NET, Supabase, React/Next.js, Expo, SwiftUI, voice agent e Docker/Dokploy. Per altro, aggiungi una skill <span class="inline-code">stack-&lt;nome&gt;</span>.</p>',
 '<summary>Does it work with my stack?</summary><p>The team is generic: it reads your <span class="inline-code">CLAUDE.md</span> and follows the conventions it finds. It also ships knowledge skills for TypeScript, .NET, Supabase, React/Next.js, Expo, SwiftUI, voice agents and Docker/Dokploy. For anything else, add a <span class="inline-code">stack-&lt;name&gt;</span> skill.</p>'),
('<summary>Perché alcuni ruoli usano Opus e altri Sonnet?</summary><p>Opus dove conta il giudizio: decidere cosa costruire (product, growth), come costruirlo (architect) e se è davvero giusto (qa, security). Sonnet dove conta eseguire bene e in fretta un piano già chiaro, con contratti definiti.</p>',
 '<summary>Why do some roles use Opus and others Sonnet?</summary><p>Opus where judgment matters: deciding what to build (product, growth), how to build it (architect) and whether it\'s really right (qa, security). Sonnet where what matters is executing a clear plan with defined contracts, well and fast.</p>'),
